IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voca-dates`
IMPORT `voca-mai-s37`
IMPORT `voca-core`

-- Victims of Crime Assistance Act 2009 (Qld) -- financial assistance from the seat of the applicant.
--
-- SEAT: the person applying for assistance: a primary, parent secondary, witness secondary or related victim of an act
-- of violence, or a person applying for funeral expense assistance. "Am I a victim who can get assistance, and in which
-- capacity? What can I get, and up to how much? By when must I apply? Will my claim wait for workers' compensation or
-- a motor accident claim? What reduces it, and what stops it? Can I get help now? How do I ask for a review? When must
-- I pay money back?" Every question is asked as that person would ask it, on facts that person could state; the scheme
-- manager's and the government assessor's judgments are facts the person answers from what they have been told. The
-- rules are in voca-core.l4 and voca-mai-s37.l4; this module builds their records from plain answers and restates no
-- rule. Inputs with the same meaning have the same name in every question, so the form can ask them once.
--
-- COVERED: an act of violence on or after 2 September 2024 (the version deposited). Questions that take the day of the
-- act answer `not covered` for an earlier act.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Victims of Crime Assistance Act 2009 -- the applicant's questions`

-- A placeholder for a date field that the question's rule does not read (the record needs a value).
`an unused date` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000

DECLARE `Amount answer` IS ONE OF
    `the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered: the act of violence happened before 2 September 2024, when transitional provisions not in the deposit may apply`

DECLARE `Special assistance answer` IS ONE OF
    `special assistance` HAS `the category of the act` IS A `Category`
                             `the category whose amount I get` IS A `Category`
                             `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no special assistance: only a primary victim gets it (s 39(h))`
    `not covered: the act of violence happened before 2 September 2024 (transitional provisions not in the deposit may apply)`

§§ `Am I a victim, and in which capacity (ss 5, 23-27)`

@export Am I a victim of an act of violence who can get victim assistance under the Victims of Crime Assistance Act 2009 (Qld), and in which capacity (primary, parent secondary, witness secondary or related victim)?
GIVEN `it happened in Queensland` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the crime or domestic violence was committed in Queensland (the death or injury may have happened anywhere)
      `it was an offence against a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what was done was an offence against the person of someone (such as an assault, sexual offence, robbery or murder), or an attempt or conspiracy to commit one, whether or not anyone has been identified, charged or convicted
      `it was lawful under an Act or in executing the law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what was done was authorised under an Act (for example a police officer acting lawfully in their duties), or done in the circumstances in Criminal Code s 31(1)(a) or (b); other excuses and defences do not count
      `it was domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was domestic violence within the Domestic and Family Violence Protection Act 2012
      `someone died or was injured as a direct result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it directly resulted in the death of, or injury to, one or more people (injury includes bodily injury, mental illness or disorder, intellectual impairment, pregnancy, disease, and for a sexual offence or domestic violence its harmful effects on the person)
      `I was injured because it was done to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured as a direct result of the act being committed against you
      `I am a parent of a child it injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a parent (including a step-parent, approved carer, or person with a parenting order or day-to-day care) of a child who was injured as a direct result of the act being committed against the child
      `I was injured on becoming aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured (for example a mental illness or disorder) as a direct result of becoming aware of the act
      `I was injured by witnessing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured as a direct result of witnessing the act, which includes hearing it being committed
      `the person it was done to died of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person the act was committed against died as a direct result of it
      `I was a family member close to the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the spouse, child, parent or step-parent, brother, sister, stepbrother or stepsister (or regarded as one under Aboriginal tradition or Island custom) of the person who died, and had a genuine personal relationship with them when they died
      `I was a dependant of the person who died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were, or would have been, entirely or substantially dependent on the income of the person who died (including their child born after their death)
      `I committed the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you committed the act of violence yourself
      `I suffered harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered physical, mental or emotional harm because of what happened
      `I was harmed intervening to help` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were harmed as a direct result of intervening to help someone who died or was harmed by the crime or domestic violence
GIVETH A `Capacity answer`
DECIDE `Am I a victim who can get assistance, and in which capacity` IS
    `the capacity answer for` `what happened` `the relationship` `the harm`
    WHERE
        `what happened` MEANS
            `What happened` WITH
                `was committed in Queensland`                                                         IS `it happened in Queensland`
                `was an offence against the person of someone, or an attempt or conspiracy to commit one` IS `it was an offence against a person`
                `was authorised under an Act, or done as mentioned in Criminal Code s 31(1)(a) or (b)` IS `it was lawful under an Act or in executing the law`
                `was domestic violence`                                                               IS `it was domestic violence`
                `directly resulted in someone's death or injury`                                      IS `someone died or was injured as a direct result`
        `the relationship` MEANS
            `Relationship to the act` WITH
                `was injured as a direct result of the act being committed against them`                IS `I was injured because it was done to me`
                `is a parent of a child injured as a direct result of the act being committed against the child` IS `I am a parent of a child it injured`
                `was injured as a direct result of becoming aware of the act`                           IS `I was injured on becoming aware of it`
                `was injured as a direct result of witnessing (seeing or hearing) the act`              IS `I was injured by witnessing it`
                `a primary victim of the act died as a direct result of it`                             IS `the person it was done to died of it`
                `is a family member of that primary victim with a genuine personal relationship with them when they died` IS `I was a family member close to the person who died`
                `is a dependant of that primary victim`                                                 IS `I was a dependant of the person who died`
                `committed the act`                                                                     IS `I committed the act`
        `the harm` MEANS
            `Harm facts` WITH
                `suffered harm`                                                                  IS `I suffered harm`
                `the crime or domestic violence was committed against them`                      IS `I was injured because it was done to me`
                `is a family member or dependant of a person who died or was harmed by it`       IS `I was a family member close to the person who died` OR `I was a dependant of the person who died` OR `I am a parent of a child it injured`
                `was harmed as a direct result of intervening to help a person who died or was harmed by it` IS `I was harmed intervening to help`
                `committed it`                                                                   IS `I committed the act`

@export What happens to my entitlement, my application or my grant of victim assistance if I die (s 24)?
GIVEN `where things stand` IS A `Stage at death` @desc Where things stand: entitled but not yet applied; applied but not decided; granted but not yet paid; or paid
GIVETH A `Death answer`
DECIDE `What happens if I die` IS `the s 24 answer for` `where things stand`

§§ `What I can get (Parts 4 to 8, Schedule 2)`

GIVEN `what the act involved` IS A `What the act involved`
      `it was a series of related crimes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I suffered a bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I suffered a mental illness or disorder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I suffered an intellectual impairment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I became pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I suffered a disease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I suffered the harmful effects of a sexual offence or domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my bodily injury is very serious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my mental illness or impairment is very serious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `treatment would make it no longer very serious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my unborn child's life was destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was infected with a life-threatening disease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was deprived of my liberty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE
      `the day of the last crime in the series` IS A DATE
      `I had an impaired capacity at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Special assistance facts`
`my special assistance facts` `what the act involved` `it was a series of related crimes` `I suffered a bodily injury` `I suffered a mental illness or disorder` `I suffered an intellectual impairment` `I became pregnant` `I suffered a disease` `I suffered the harmful effects of a sexual offence or domestic violence` `my bodily injury is very serious` `my mental illness or impairment is very serious` `treatment would make it no longer very serious` `my unborn child's life was destroyed` `I was infected with a life-threatening disease` `I was deprived of my liberty` `my date of birth` `the day of the act of violence` `the day of the last crime in the series` `I had an impaired capacity at the time` MEANS
    `Special assistance facts` WITH
        `what the act involved, at its most serious`                                     IS `what the act involved`
        `the act was a series of related crimes`                                          IS `it was a series of related crimes`
        `the injury`                                                                      IS `Injury kinds` WITH
            `bodily injury`                                                     IS `I suffered a bodily injury`
            `mental illness or disorder`                                        IS `I suffered a mental illness or disorder`
            `intellectual impairment`                                           IS `I suffered an intellectual impairment`
            `pregnancy`                                                         IS `I became pregnant`
            `disease`                                                           IS `I suffered a disease`
            `the adverse impacts of a sexual offence or domestic violence in s 27(1)(f)` IS `I suffered the harmful effects of a sexual offence or domestic violence`
            `an aggravation of an injury of those kinds, caused by the act`     IS FALSE -- not read by Schedule 2
        `a bodily injury caused a loss or impairment of a bodily function, or disfigurement, and a permanent and significant reduction in quality of life or is otherwise very serious` IS `my bodily injury is very serious`
        `a mental illness or disorder, or intellectual impairment, caused a permanent and significant reduction in quality of life or is otherwise very serious` IS `my mental illness or impairment is very serious`
        `that injury would stop being very serious if it were treated`                    IS `treatment would make it no longer very serious`
        `a bodily injury destroyed the life of the victim's unborn child`                 IS `my unborn child's life was destroyed`
        `was infected with a life-threatening disease, such as HIV`                      IS `I was infected with a life-threatening disease`
        `suffered a deprivation of liberty as a direct result of the act`                 IS `I was deprived of my liberty`
        `was a child under 16 when the act, or one of the acts in the series, was committed` IS `someone born on` `my date of birth` `is under` 16 `on` `the day of the act of violence`
        `was over 60 when the act, or one of the acts in the series, was committed`       IS `someone born on` `my date of birth` `is over` 60 `on` `the day of the last crime in the series`
        `had an impaired capacity when the act, or one of the acts in the series, was committed` IS `I had an impaired capacity at the time`

@export As a primary victim, what category is the act of violence, and how much special assistance can I get (Schedule 2)?
GIVEN `I am applying as` IS A `Victim capacity` @desc The capacity you are applying in: primary victim, parent secondary victim, witness secondary victim or related victim
      `what the act involved` IS A `What the act involved` @desc The most serious thing the act of violence involved, from the Schedule 2 list (for a series of related crimes, the most serious crime in the series)
      `it was a series of related crimes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act of violence was a series of related crimes: 2 or more crimes against you at about the same time, or over a period by the same person or group, or otherwise related, before any assistance was granted for the earlier ones
      `I suffered a bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered a bodily injury as a direct result
      `I suffered a mental illness or disorder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered a mental illness or disorder (cognitive, neurological or psychiatric) as a direct result
      `I suffered an intellectual impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered an intellectual impairment as a direct result
      `I became pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became pregnant as a direct result
      `I suffered a disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you contracted a disease as a direct result
      `I suffered the harmful effects of a sexual offence or domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a sexual offence or domestic violence, whether you suffered its harmful effects together (sense of violation, reduced self-worth, increased fear or insecurity, adverse effect on relationships and feelings, lost physical capacity)
      `my bodily injury is very serious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a bodily injury caused a loss or impairment of a bodily function (including capacity to have children) or disfigurement, and has permanently and significantly reduced your quality of life or is otherwise very serious
      `my mental illness or impairment is very serious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a mental illness or disorder, or intellectual impairment, has permanently and significantly reduced your quality of life or is otherwise very serious
      `treatment would make it no longer very serious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that injury, illness or impairment would stop being very serious with medical or other treatment
      `my unborn child's life was destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a bodily injury from the act destroyed the life of your unborn child
      `I was infected with a life-threatening disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were infected, as a direct result, with a life-threatening disease such as HIV
      `I was deprived of my liberty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered a deprivation of liberty as a direct result of the act
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO 8601, e.g. 1990-05-17)
      `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened (for a series of related crimes, the day of the first crime in it), ISO 8601
      `the day of the last crime in the series` IS A DATE @desc For a series of related crimes, the day of the last crime in it; for a single act, the same day as the act
      `I had an impaired capacity at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had an impaired capacity (within the Guardianship and Administration Act 2000) when the act, or one of the crimes in the series, was committed
GIVETH A `Special assistance answer`
DECIDE `What special assistance can I get` IS
    IF NOT (`the act of violence is covered by this encoding` `the day of the act of violence`)
    THEN `not covered: the act of violence happened before 2 September 2024 (transitional provisions not in the deposit may apply)`
    ELSE IF NOT (`I am applying as` EQUALS `primary victim`)
         THEN `no special assistance: only a primary victim gets it (s 39(h))`
         ELSE `special assistance` (`the category (Schedule 2 s 3) of an act involving` `what the act involved`) (`the category whose amount is paid (Schedule 2 s 1)` `the facts`) (`the special assistance payable (Schedule 2)` `the facts`)
    WHERE
        `the facts` MEANS `my special assistance facts` `what the act involved` `it was a series of related crimes` `I suffered a bodily injury` `I suffered a mental illness or disorder` `I suffered an intellectual impairment` `I became pregnant` `I suffered a disease` `I suffered the harmful effects of a sexual offence or domestic violence` `my bodily injury is very serious` `my mental illness or impairment is very serious` `treatment would make it no longer very serious` `my unborn child's life was destroyed` `I was infected with a life-threatening disease` `I was deprived of my liberty` `my date of birth` `the day of the act of violence` `the day of the last crime in the series` `I had an impaired capacity at the time`

@export What is the most victim assistance I can be granted, before any reduction, in the capacity I am applying in (Parts 3 to 7)?
GIVEN `I am applying as` IS A `Victim capacity` @desc The capacity you are applying in: primary victim, parent secondary victim, witness secondary victim or related victim (only one, even if you are a victim in more than one)
      `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened (for a series of related crimes, the day of the first crime in it), ISO 8601
      `the act caused a death by murder, manslaughter or driving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a witness: whether the act involved murder, unlawful striking causing death, manslaughter or dangerous driving causing death (a more serious act of violence)
      `exceptional circumstances exist for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the government assessor accepts that, because of your circumstances or the nature of the act, it has had an unusual, special or out of the ordinary effect on you (s 28)
      `my counselling expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Reasonable counselling expenses you have incurred or are reasonably likely to incur as a direct result, in Australian dollars
      `my medical expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Reasonable medical and ambulance expenses you have incurred or are reasonably likely to incur as a direct result, in Australian dollars
      `my incidental travel expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Reasonable travel expenses for counselling or treatment at least 20 km away (or 150 km in 7 days), or for an examination the assessor asked for, in Australian dollars
      `my report expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Reasonable expenses for reports from a counsellor or health practitioner for your application, in Australian dollars
      `my loss of earnings in the 2 years` IS A NUMBER @desc Earnings you lost, or are reasonably likely to lose, as a direct result, in the 2 years after the act (or after becoming aware of it, for a parent), in Australian dollars (for a parent or witness, counted only with exceptional circumstances)
      `my clothing lost or damaged` IS A NUMBER @desc For a primary victim: the cost of clothing you were wearing that was lost or damaged in the act, in Australian dollars
      `my other recovery expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc Other reasonable expenses to significantly help you recover, such as relocation or securing your home or business, in Australian dollars (counted only with exceptional circumstances; not for a witness to a less serious act)
      `what the person who died would have given me in 2 years` IS A NUMBER @desc For a related victim: what you would have been reasonably likely to receive from the person who died in the 2 years after their death, in Australian dollars
      `the amount I ask for distress` IS A NUMBER @desc For a related victim: the amount for the distress you have suffered or are likely to suffer as a direct result of the death, in Australian dollars (up to $15,000)
      `funeral expense assistance granted to me for the act` IS A NUMBER @desc For a witness or related victim: any funeral expense assistance already granted to you for this act, in Australian dollars (it is taken off the limit)
      `my legal costs of applying` IS A NUMBER @desc Legal costs charged to you by a law practice for applying for assistance, in Australian dollars
      `I am paid workers' compensation for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been paid compensation under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 for the injury or death
      `the workers' compensation lump sum paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc For a primary victim: any lump sum compensation paid to you under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `the workers' compensation paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc For a related victim: the compensation paid to you under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 for the death, in Australian dollars
      `what the act involved` IS A `What the act involved` @desc For a primary victim: the most serious thing the act of violence involved, from the Schedule 2 list (for a series of related crimes, the most serious crime in the series)
      `it was a series of related crimes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act of violence was a series of related crimes: 2 or more crimes against you at about the same time, or over a period by the same person or group, or otherwise related, before any assistance was granted for the earlier ones
      `I suffered a bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered a bodily injury as a direct result
      `I suffered a mental illness or disorder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered a mental illness or disorder (cognitive, neurological or psychiatric) as a direct result
      `I suffered an intellectual impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered an intellectual impairment as a direct result
      `I became pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became pregnant as a direct result
      `I suffered a disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you contracted a disease as a direct result
      `I suffered the harmful effects of a sexual offence or domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a sexual offence or domestic violence, whether you suffered its harmful effects together (sense of violation, reduced self-worth, increased fear or insecurity, adverse effect on relationships and feelings, lost physical capacity)
      `my bodily injury is very serious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a bodily injury caused a loss or impairment of a bodily function (including capacity to have children) or disfigurement, and has permanently and significantly reduced your quality of life or is otherwise very serious
      `my mental illness or impairment is very serious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a mental illness or disorder, or intellectual impairment, has permanently and significantly reduced your quality of life or is otherwise very serious
      `treatment would make it no longer very serious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that injury, illness or impairment would stop being very serious with medical or other treatment
      `my unborn child's life was destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a bodily injury from the act destroyed the life of your unborn child
      `I was infected with a life-threatening disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were infected, as a direct result, with a life-threatening disease such as HIV
      `I was deprived of my liberty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered a deprivation of liberty as a direct result of the act
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO 8601, e.g. 1990-05-17)
      `the day of the last crime in the series` IS A DATE @desc For a series of related crimes, the day of the last crime in it; for a single act, the same day as the act
      `I had an impaired capacity at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had an impaired capacity (within the Guardianship and Administration Act 2000) when the act, or one of the crimes in the series, was committed
GIVETH AN `Amount answer`
DECIDE `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` IS
    IF NOT (`the act of violence is covered by this encoding` `the day of the act of violence`)
    THEN `not covered: the act of violence happened before 2 September 2024, when transitional provisions not in the deposit may apply`
    ELSE `the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` (`the most victim assistance that can be granted for` `the claim`)
    WHERE
        `the special assistance` MEANS
            IF `I am applying as` EQUALS `primary victim`
            THEN `the special assistance payable (Schedule 2)` (`my special assistance facts` `what the act involved` `it was a series of related crimes` `I suffered a bodily injury` `I suffered a mental illness or disorder` `I suffered an intellectual impairment` `I became pregnant` `I suffered a disease` `I suffered the harmful effects of a sexual offence or domestic violence` `my bodily injury is very serious` `my mental illness or impairment is very serious` `treatment would make it no longer very serious` `my unborn child's life was destroyed` `I was infected with a life-threatening disease` `I was deprived of my liberty` `my date of birth` `the day of the act of violence` `the day of the last crime in the series` `I had an impaired capacity at the time`)
            ELSE 0
        `the claim` MEANS
            `Assistance claim` WITH
                `the capacity applied in`                                         IS `I am applying as`
                `the act is a more serious act of violence`                       IS `the act caused a death by murder, manslaughter or driving`
                `exceptional circumstances exist for the victim (s 28)`           IS `exceptional circumstances exist for me`
                `counselling expenses`                                            IS `my counselling expenses`
                `medical expenses`                                                IS `my medical expenses`
                `incidental travel expenses`                                      IS `my incidental travel expenses`
                `report expenses`                                                 IS `my report expenses`
                `loss of earnings in the 2 years`                                 IS `my loss of earnings in the 2 years`
                `loss of or damage to clothing worn at the time`                  IS `my clothing lost or damaged`
                `other expenses to significantly help recovery`                   IS `my other recovery expenses`
                `what the primary victim would have given in the 2 years after death` IS `what the person who died would have given me in 2 years`
                `distress amount`                                                 IS `the amount I ask for distress`
                `special assistance`                                              IS `the special assistance`
                `funeral expense assistance granted to this victim for the act`  IS `funeral expense assistance granted to me for the act`
                `legal costs of applying`                                         IS `my legal costs of applying`
                `is paid compensation under the Workers' Compensation Act`        IS `I am paid workers' compensation for it`
                `lump sum compensation paid under the Workers' Compensation Act`  IS `the workers' compensation lump sum paid to me`
                `compensation paid under the Workers' Compensation Act`           IS `the workers' compensation paid to me`

@export How much funeral expense assistance can I get for the funeral of a person who died because of an act of violence, or of an unborn child whose life it destroyed (s 50)?
GIVEN `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened, ISO 8601
      `I pay for the funeral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have incurred, or are reasonably likely to incur, funeral expenses for a person who died as a direct result of the act, or for an unborn child whose life it destroyed
      `I committed the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you committed the act of violence yourself
      `the funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc The funeral expenses you have incurred or are reasonably likely to incur, in Australian dollars
      `funeral expense assistance already granted to others` IS A NUMBER @desc Funeral expense assistance already granted to other people for the same person's (or unborn child's) funeral, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH AN `Amount answer`
DECIDE `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` IS
    IF NOT (`the act of violence is covered by this encoding` `the day of the act of violence`)
    THEN `not covered: the act of violence happened before 2 September 2024, when transitional provisions not in the deposit may apply`
    ELSE `the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` (`the most funeral expense assistance (s 50(3)-(4))` `the facts`)
    WHERE
        `the facts` MEANS
            `Funeral facts` WITH
                `incurs funeral expenses for a primary victim who died as a direct result of the act, or for an unborn child whose life it destroyed` IS `I pay for the funeral`
                `committed the act`                                                     IS `I committed the act`
                `the funeral expenses`                                                  IS `the funeral expenses`
                `funeral expense assistance already granted to others for the same funeral` IS `funeral expense assistance already granted to others`

§§ `Applying (ss 51, 52, 54 to 60)`

@export Who may make my application for victim assistance (s 51)?
GIVEN `I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the victim is a child (under 18)
      `I am at least 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the victim is at least 12 years old
      `I have a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the victim is represented by an Australian legal practitioner or government legal officer
      `I am an adult with an impaired capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the victim is an adult with an impaired capacity (within the Guardianship and Administration Act 2000)
      `I have a guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the victim has a guardian appointed under the Guardianship and Administration Act 2000
      `I have an administrator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the victim has an administrator appointed under the Guardianship and Administration Act 2000
      `I have an attorney under an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the victim has appointed an attorney under an enduring power of attorney
      `I need help to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the victim (an adult without impaired capacity) needs help to make the application, for example because they do not understand English
GIVETH A LIST OF `Who may apply`
DECIDE `Who may make my application` IS
    `who may make the application under s 51 for` (`Applicant situation` WITH
        `is a child`                                         IS `I am under 18`
        `is at least 12`                                     IS `I am at least 12`
        `is represented by a lawyer`                         IS `I have a lawyer`
        `is an adult with an impaired capacity`              IS `I am an adult with an impaired capacity`
        `has a guardian`                                     IS `I have a guardian`
        `has an administrator`                               IS `I have an administrator`
        `has appointed an attorney under an enduring power of attorney` IS `I have an attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
        `needs help to make the application`                 IS `I need help to apply`)

@export Does my application for victim assistance meet the form requirements (s 52)?
GIVEN `it is on the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application is on the approved form
      `it has supporting documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether documents supporting the application are attached
      `it gives consent to obtain information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it contains the consent for the government assessor to obtain medical information and information about other payments (ss 74, 77)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my application meet the form requirements` IF
    `the application meets s 52` `it is on the approved form` `it has supporting documents` `it gives consent to obtain information`

@export By when must I apply for victim assistance, and am I in time (ss 34, 54)?
GIVEN `I am applying as` IS A `Victim capacity` @desc The capacity you are applying in: primary victim, parent secondary victim, witness secondary victim or related victim
      `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened (for a series of related crimes, the day of the first crime in it), ISO 8601
      `the day the person who died died` IS A DATE @desc For a related victim: the day the person the act was committed against died; otherwise any date
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO 8601, e.g. 1990-05-17)
      `I am entitled to workers' compensation for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to compensation under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 for the injury or death (for example, the act happened at work)
      `I have made a workers' compensation application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied for compensation under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003
      `my workers' compensation application is finally dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your total entitlement to workers' compensation has been decided (rejected, a lump sum offer accepted or rejected, or the entitlement stopped)
      `the day it was finally dealt with` IS A DATE @desc The day your workers' compensation application was finally dealt with; otherwise any date
      `the scheme manager approved my applying without one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme manager has approved your applying without first making a workers' compensation application (s 34(4))
      `the scheme manager extended my time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme manager has extended the time for you to apply
      `the day my time was extended to` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended time; otherwise any date
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied, or will apply, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Time to apply answer`
DECIDE `By when must I apply for victim assistance` IS
    `the victim assistance time answer for` (`Application timing` WITH
        `the capacity applied in`                                     IS `I am applying as`
        `the day of the act of violence`                              IS `the day of the act of violence`
        `the day the primary victim died`                             IS `the day the person who died died`
        `the victim's date of birth`                                  IS `my date of birth`
        `is entitled to compensation under the Workers' Compensation Act` IS `I am entitled to workers' compensation for it`
        `has made a workers' compensation application`                IS `I have made a workers' compensation application`
        `the workers' compensation application has been finally dealt with` IS `my workers' compensation application is finally dealt with`
        `the day it was finally dealt with`                           IS `the day it was finally dealt with`
        `has the scheme manager's approval under s 34(4)`             IS `the scheme manager approved my applying without one`
        `the scheme manager has extended the time`                    IS `the scheme manager extended my time`
        `the day the time was extended to`                            IS `the day my time was extended to`) `the day I apply`

@export By when must I apply for funeral expense assistance, and am I in time (s 58)?
GIVEN `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE @desc The day the act of violence happened, ISO 8601
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE @desc The day the person died, or the day the unborn child's life was destroyed, ISO 8601
      `the scheme manager extended my time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme manager has extended the time for you to apply
      `the day my time was extended to` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended time; otherwise any date
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied, or will apply, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Time to apply answer`
DECIDE `By when must I apply for funeral expense assistance` IS
    `the funeral expense time answer for` `the day of the act of violence` `the day of the death` `the scheme manager extended my time` `the day my time was extended to` `the day I apply`

@export Can I still withdraw my application, or change it, including the capacity I am applying in (ss 59, 60)?
GIVEN `my application has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the government assessor has decided your application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still withdraw or change my application` IF
    `the applicant may withdraw or amend the application (ss 59, 60)` `my application has been decided`

§§ `If I am entitled to workers' compensation, or the act involved a motor vehicle (Parts 3, 3A, 3B)`

-- Situation: only for a person entitled to workers' compensation for the injury, or where the act of violence involved
-- a motor vehicle accident. The form can ask "Did this happen at work, or involve a motor vehicle?" first.

@export If I am entitled to workers' compensation for the injury or death, may I apply for victim assistance yet (s 34)?
GIVEN `I am applying as` IS A `Victim capacity` @desc The capacity you are applying in: primary victim, parent secondary victim, witness secondary victim or related victim
      `I am entitled to workers' compensation for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to compensation under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003 for the injury or death (for example, the act happened at work)
      `I have made a workers' compensation application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied for compensation under the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003
      `my workers' compensation application is finally dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your total entitlement to workers' compensation has been decided (rejected, a lump sum offer accepted or rejected, or the entitlement stopped)
      `the scheme manager approved my applying without one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme manager has approved your applying without first making a workers' compensation application (s 34(4))
GIVETH A `Workers' compensation answer`
DECIDE `May I apply yet, if I am entitled to workers' compensation` IS
    `the Part 3 answer for` (`Application timing` WITH
        `the capacity applied in`                                     IS `I am applying as`
        `the day of the act of violence`                              IS `an unused date`
        `the day the primary victim died`                             IS `an unused date`
        `the victim's date of birth`                                  IS `an unused date`
        `is entitled to compensation under the Workers' Compensation Act` IS `I am entitled to workers' compensation for it`
        `has made a workers' compensation application`                IS `I have made a workers' compensation application`
        `the workers' compensation application has been finally dealt with` IS `my workers' compensation application is finally dealt with`
        `the day it was finally dealt with`                           IS `an unused date`
        `has the scheme manager's approval under s 34(4)`             IS `the scheme manager approved my applying without one`
        `the scheme manager has extended the time`                    IS FALSE -- not read by s 34(1)
        `the day the time was extended to`                            IS `an unused date`)

@export By when must I give notice of my motor accident claim, and is my claim barred (Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994, s 37(2)-(3))?
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor vehicle accident, ISO 8601
      `the vehicle can be identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor vehicle at fault can be identified (if not, the claim is against the Nominal Defendant)
      `my symptoms were immediately apparent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the symptoms of your injury were immediately apparent
      `the day my symptoms first appeared` IS A DATE @desc If the symptoms were not immediately apparent, the day they first appeared; otherwise any date
      `I have consulted a lawyer about a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have consulted a lawyer about the possibility of making a claim
      `the day I first consulted a lawyer` IS A DATE @desc The day you first consulted a lawyer about it; otherwise any date
      `I have given notice of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given written notice of the claim to the insurer (or the Nominal Defendant)
      `the day I gave notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave notice of the claim; otherwise any date
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Motor accident notice answer`
DECIDE `By when must I give notice of my motor accident claim` IS
    `the MAI s 37 answer for` (`Motor accident notice facts` WITH
        `the day of the accident`                                    IS `the day of the accident`
        `the motor vehicle can be identified`                        IS `the vehicle can be identified`
        `symptoms of the injury were immediately apparent`           IS `my symptoms were immediately apparent`
        `the day symptoms of the injury first appeared`              IS `the day my symptoms first appeared`
        `the claimant has consulted a lawyer about a possible claim` IS `I have consulted a lawyer about a claim`
        `the day the claimant first consulted a lawyer about it`     IS `the day I first consulted a lawyer`) `I have given notice of the claim` `the day I gave notice` `today`

@export Will the decision on my victim assistance application wait for my motor accident claim (ss 36A to 36F)?
GIVEN `someone was personally injured in a motor vehicle incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act of violence resulted in an incident involving a motor vehicle from which a liability for personal injury arose
      `the liability is covered by CTP insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that liability is covered by compulsory third-party (CTP) insurance under the statutory insurance scheme, including through the Nominal Defendant
      `I have made or can make a motor accident claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made, or are or were entitled to make, a claim under the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994
      `my motor accident claim` IS A `Motor accident claim state` @desc Where your motor accident claim stands: not made; made and not finally dealt with; the insurer denied liability; an offer or counter offer of settlement accepted; or a court proceeding on it has ended, including appeals
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE @desc The day of the motor vehicle accident, ISO 8601
      `the vehicle can be identified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the motor vehicle at fault can be identified (if not, the claim is against the Nominal Defendant)
      `I have given notice of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given written notice of the claim to the insurer (or the Nominal Defendant)
      `the day I gave notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave notice of the claim; otherwise any date
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, ISO 8601
      `I tried to give late notice without success` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you tried, without success, to give notice of a motor accident claim after the time for it had passed
      `the scheme manager accepts my excuse for not claiming in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme manager is satisfied you have a reasonable excuse for not making the motor accident claim in time
GIVETH A `Motor accident deferral answer`
DECIDE `Will the decision wait for my motor accident claim` IS
    `the Part 3A answer for` (`Motor accident facts` WITH
        `the act resulted in a motor vehicle accident (MAI s 4)`    IS `the incident is a motor vehicle accident (MAI s 4)` `someone was personally injured in a motor vehicle incident` `the liability is covered by CTP insurance`
        `has made, or is or was entitled to make, a motor accident claim` IS `I have made or can make a motor accident claim`
        `the claim`                                                 IS `my motor accident claim`
        `the claim is barred under MAI s 37(3)`                     IS `the claim is barred under MAI s 37(3)` `the notice facts` `I have given notice of the claim` `the day I gave notice` `today`
        `tried unsuccessfully under MAI s 37(3) to give late notice of the claim` IS `I tried to give late notice without success`
        `the scheme manager is satisfied of a reasonable excuse for not claiming within the MAI s 37(2) period` IS `the scheme manager accepts my excuse for not claiming in time`)
    WHERE
        -- The s 37(3) bar reads only the day of the accident and whether the vehicle can be identified; the symptom and
        -- lawyer fields are placeholders.
        `the notice facts` MEANS
            `Motor accident notice facts` WITH
                `the day of the accident`                                    IS `the day of the accident`
                `the motor vehicle can be identified`                        IS `the vehicle can be identified`
                `symptoms of the injury were immediately apparent`           IS TRUE
                `the day symptoms of the injury first appeared`              IS `the day of the accident`
                `the claimant has consulted a lawyer about a possible claim` IS FALSE
                `the day the claimant first consulted a lawyer about it`     IS `an unused date`

@export As a primary victim, can the decision on my application wait for my NIISQ application, and for how long (ss 36G to 36J)?
GIVEN `I am applying as` IS A `Victim capacity` @desc The capacity you are applying in: primary victim, parent secondary victim, witness secondary victim or related victim
      `an NIISQ application has been or can be made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or someone else has made, or is entitled to make, an application to participate in the National Injury Insurance Scheme, Queensland (NIISQ) for your injury
      `my NIISQ application has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the National Injury Insurance Agency has decided the NIISQ application
      `my decision is deferred for a motor accident claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision on your application is also deferred for a motor accident claim (see the motor accident question)
      `the day I applied for victim assistance` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied for victim assistance, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `NIISQ deferral answer`
DECIDE `Can the decision wait for my NIISQ application` IS
    `the Part 3B answer for` (`NIISQ facts` WITH
        `the capacity applied in`                                  IS `I am applying as`
        `an NIISQ application has been made, or can be made, for the injury` IS `an NIISQ application has been or can be made`
        `the NIISQ application has been decided`                   IS `my NIISQ application has been decided`
        `the decision is also deferred for a motor accident claim (s 36D or 36E)` IS `my decision is deferred for a motor accident claim`
        `the day the victim assistance application was made`       IS `the day I applied for victim assistance`)

§§ `What can stop or reduce a grant (ss 21, 78 to 82, 85, 86)`

@export Is anything in the Act stopping a grant of assistance to me: eligibility, my part in the act, the primary victim's criminal activity, reporting, or helping police (ss 21, 78 to 82)?
GIVEN `I am eligible for the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are eligible for the assistance you applied for (see the victim and funeral questions)
      `I committed the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you committed the act of violence yourself
      `I conspired with the person who did it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you conspired with the person who committed the act of violence
      `I am the primary victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying as the primary victim (the person the act was committed against)
      `the act was mainly because of the primary victim's criminal activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only or main reason the act was committed against the primary victim was their involvement, at the time or before, in a criminal activity
      `I knew or should have known of that activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are not the primary victim: whether you were, or ought reasonably to have been, aware of the primary victim's involvement in that criminal activity
      `I knew of it only because I witnessed the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were aware of it only because you witnessed the act of violence
      `it was reported to police` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act of violence has been reported to a police officer
      `it was reported to a counsellor, psychologist, doctor or domestic violence service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has been reported to the primary victim's counsellor, psychologist or doctor, or to a domestic violence service
      `it involved a sexual offence or domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act of violence involved a sexual offence or domestic violence
      `the offender was in a position of power, influence or trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who committed it was in a position of power, influence or trust in relation to the primary victim (such as a parent, spouse or carer)
      `the primary victim was a child or has an impaired capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the primary victim was a child when the act was committed, or has an impaired capacity
      `the primary victim is being threatened or intimidated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the primary victim is being threatened or intimidated by the person who committed it or by someone else
      `there is a reasonable excuse for not reporting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the government assessor would accept a reasonable excuse for the act not being reported
      `I did not help the police investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not give reasonable assistance in the police investigation of the act (if there was one)
      `the act was a crime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act of violence was a crime or series of related crimes (rather than domestic violence that was not a crime)
      `I did not help the arrest or prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not give reasonable assistance in the arrest or prosecution of the person who committed, or allegedly committed, the act
      `that prevented the arrest or prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your not helping prevented the arrest or prosecution
      `I had a reasonable excuse for not helping` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the government assessor would accept that you had a reasonable excuse for not helping (your age, impaired capacity, a sexual offence, a person in a position of power or trust, domestic violence, threats or intimidation, the nature of your injury, or other special circumstances)
GIVETH A `Restriction answer`
DECIDE `Is anything stopping a grant to me` IS
    `the restriction answer for` (`Restriction facts` WITH
        `is eligible for the assistance under chapter 3`                                IS `I am eligible for the assistance`
        `committed the act`                                                             IS `I committed the act`
        `conspired with the person who committed the act`                               IS `I conspired with the person who did it`
        `is the primary victim`                                                         IS `I am the primary victim`
        `the only or main reason the act was committed against the primary victim was the primary victim's involvement in a criminal activity` IS `the act was mainly because of the primary victim's criminal activity`
        `was, or ought reasonably to have been, aware of that involvement`             IS `I knew or should have known of that activity`
        `was aware of it only because of witnessing the act`                            IS `I knew of it only because I witnessed the act`
        `the act was reported to a police officer`                                      IS `it was reported to police`
        `the act was reported to the primary victim's counsellor, psychologist or doctor, or to a domestic violence service` IS `it was reported to a counsellor, psychologist, doctor or domestic violence service`
        `the act involved a sexual offence or domestic violence`                        IS `it involved a sexual offence or domestic violence`
        `the person who committed it was in a position of power, influence or trust in relation to the primary victim` IS `the offender was in a position of power, influence or trust`
        `the primary victim was a child when it was committed, or has an impaired capacity` IS `the primary victim was a child or has an impaired capacity`
        `the primary victim is being threatened or intimidated`                         IS `the primary victim is being threatened or intimidated`
        `there is a reasonable excuse for the act not being reported`                   IS `there is a reasonable excuse for not reporting`
        `did not give reasonable assistance in the police investigation`                IS `I did not help the police investigation`
        `the act is a crime or a series of related crimes`                              IS `the act was a crime`
        `did not give reasonable assistance in the arrest or prosecution`               IS `I did not help the arrest or prosecution`
        `that failure prevented the arrest or prosecution`                              IS `that prevented the arrest or prosecution`
        `had a reasonable excuse for not giving the assistance`                         IS `I had a reasonable excuse for not helping`)

@export How much will I be paid after the reductions for my own conduct, for other payments for the same act, and for interim assistance already paid (ss 85, 86, 100)?
GIVEN `the assistance otherwise payable` IS A NUMBER @desc The assistance that would otherwise be payable to you, in Australian dollars (from the most-you-can-be-granted question, or the government assessor's notice)
      `the reduction for my conduct, in percent` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage by which the government assessor reduces your assistance because your own conduct contributed to your injury (s 85), e.g. 25; 0 if none
      `other payments for the same act` IS A NUMBER @desc Payments you have received or will receive for the act from another source (workers' compensation, CTP insurance, NIISQ, Medicare, insurance, superannuation, damages, a mediated agreement), in Australian dollars; not a National Redress Scheme payment
      `the part of them not for expenses I can claim` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of those payments the government assessor accepts was made for a purpose that does not include paying you for expenses you can get assistance for, in Australian dollars (0 if unsure)
      `interim assistance paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc Interim assistance already paid to you for this application, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will I be paid after reductions` IS
    `the assistance still to be paid after interim assistance` (`the assistance after ss 85 and 86` `the assistance otherwise payable` (`the reduction for my conduct, in percent` DIVIDED BY 100) `other payments for the same act` `the part of them not for expenses I can claim`) `interim assistance paid to me`

§§ `While my application is open (Parts 11 and 14, s 141A)`

@export Can I get interim assistance for urgent expenses while my application is being decided, and how much (ss 97, 98)?
GIVEN `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied for victim assistance or funeral expense assistance
      `my application has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the government assessor has decided your application
      `I have urgent and immediate expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have incurred, or will incur before the decision, urgent and immediate expenses of a kind assistance can cover
      `I asked for interim assistance in my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked for interim assistance in your application
      `the assessor accepts the expenses cannot wait` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the government assessor is reasonably satisfied you need to incur the expenses before your application is decided
      `my urgent expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc The urgent expenses, in Australian dollars
GIVETH AN `Interim answer`
DECIDE `Can I get interim assistance` IS
    `the interim answer for` (`Interim facts` WITH
        `has applied for victim or funeral expense assistance`                   IS `I have applied`
        `the application has been decided`                                       IS `my application has been decided`
        `has urgent and immediate expenses before the decision, of a kind assistance can cover` IS `I have urgent and immediate expenses`
        `asked for interim assistance in the application`                        IS `I asked for interim assistance in my application`
        `the government assessor is reasonably satisfied the expenses must be incurred before the decision` IS `the assessor accepts the expenses cannot wait`
        `the urgent expenses`                                                    IS `my urgent expenses`)

@export Will my application lapse if I do not keep in contact with the government assessor (s 61)?
GIVEN `I have been given a lapse notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the government assessor has given you a notice that your application will lapse unless you make contact within 6 months
      `the day of the lapse notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice was given; otherwise any date
      `I have made contact since the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have contacted the government assessor, the scheme manager or another assessor acting for them since the notice
      `the day I made contact, or today` IS A DATE @desc The day you made contact, or today if you have not, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Lapse answer`
DECIDE `Will my application lapse` IS
    `the s 61 answer for` `I have been given a lapse notice` `the day of the lapse notice` `I have made contact since the notice` `the day I made contact, or today`

@export By when must I tell the scheme manager about a payment I receive for the act, such as workers' compensation, insurance or damages (ss 89(2), 98(2), 141A)?
GIVEN `where my application is` IS A `Payment stage` @desc Where your application was when you received the payment: before it was decided and before any interim assistance; after interim assistance, before the decision; or after assistance was granted
      `the day assistance was granted` IS A DATE @desc If assistance has been granted, the day it was granted; otherwise any date
      `the day I received the payment` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the payment, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Payment notice answer`
DECIDE `By when must I tell the scheme manager about a payment` IS
    `the payment notice answer for` `where my application is` `the day assistance was granted` `the day I received the payment`

§§ `After the decision (Parts 15, 17 and 18, s 100)`

@export Can I apply to change the amount or conditions of my grant of assistance, and by when (s 101)?
GIVEN `my circumstances have changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your circumstances have changed, or are likely to change, since the grant
      `the day assistance was granted` IS A DATE @desc The day the assistance was originally granted, ISO 8601
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (ISO 8601, e.g. 1990-05-17)
      `the day I apply to amend` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied, or will apply, to amend the grant, ISO 8601
      `amendment applications already this year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many applications to amend this grant you have already made this calendar year
      `the scheme manager allows another this year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme manager is reasonably satisfied that exceptional circumstances allow another application this calendar year
      `I was given an amendment notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme manager has given you a notice proposing to amend the grant for an uncounted payment (Part 15, Division 2)
GIVETH AN `Amendment answer`
DECIDE `Can I apply to amend my grant` IS
    `the s 101 answer for` (`Amendment facts` WITH
        `my circumstances have changed or are likely to change`      IS `my circumstances have changed`
        `the day assistance was originally granted`                  IS `the day assistance was granted`
        `my date of birth`                                           IS `my date of birth`
        `the day of the amendment application`                       IS `the day I apply to amend`
        `applications to amend already made this calendar year`      IS `amendment applications already this year`
        `the scheme manager accepts exceptional circumstances for another this year` IS `the scheme manager allows another this year`
        `I have been given an amendment notice under Division 2`     IS `I was given an amendment notice`)

@export By when must I ask for an internal review of a decision on my application, and what comes after it (ss 124, 125)?
GIVEN `the decision is reviewable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision is one listed in Schedule 1 (for example refusing assistance, the amount granted, a condition, refusing an extension of time, deferring a decision, or refusing interim assistance)
      `the day I was given notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given notice of the decision, ISO 8601
      `the scheme manager extended my time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme manager has extended the time for you to apply
      `the day my time was extended to` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended time; otherwise any date
      `the day I apply for review` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied, or will apply, for review, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Review answer`
DECIDE `By when must I ask for an internal review` IS
    `the s 124 answer for` `the decision is reviewable` `the day I was given notice of the decision` `the scheme manager extended my time` `the day my time was extended to` `the day I apply for review`

@export How much must I pay back to the State: interim assistance, assistance after an amendment or review, or after a fraud conviction (ss 100, 106G, 123, 126)?
GIVEN `why I may have to pay back` IS A `Refund reason` @desc Why a refund may be owed: interim assistance more than the grant, or the application refused (s 100); the grant amended for an uncounted payment (s 106G); a fraud conviction about the application (s 123); or the grant reduced on review (s 126)
      `the amount paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc The assistance (or interim assistance) already paid to you, in Australian dollars
      `the assistance granted now` IS A NUMBER @desc The assistance granted to you after the decision, amendment or review, in Australian dollars (0 if refused)
      `my application was refused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For interim assistance: whether your application was refused
      `the prosecution proved the grant rested on the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a fraud conviction: whether the prosecution proved the assistance was granted on the basis of the acts or omissions that were the offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I pay back` IS
    `the refund owed to the State for` `why I may have to pay back` `the amount paid to me` `the assistance granted now` `my application was refused` `the prosecution proved the grant rested on the offence`
